  "original_branch": "partner/dist-B",
  "scope": "For all nonempty finite simple undirected graphs, gp^-(G square H)>=min(5,gp^-G,gp^-H), with no order, diameter or connectedness restriction. For every r>=6, the companion connected family has min(gp^-G_r,gp^-H_r)=r and product lower-GP exactly 5. Complete-graph examples for r=1,...,5 show that min(r,5) is the optimal universal lower bound depending only on the smaller factor parameter. The original-conjecture refutation and sharp replacement are one combined result. Source: [arXiv:2404.19451v1 Conjecture 2.10](https://arxiv.org/html/2404.19451v1), [final paper Conjecture 3](https://oro.open.ac.uk/98050/9/98050final.pdf), DOI 10.22049/cco.2024.29171.1879.",
  "status": "independently reviewed written mathematics; novelty unconfirmed; no all-parameter Lean",
  "integration_validation": "exact hashes, Python AST, JSON and dependency closure; no mathematical replay",
